{
  "_comment": "The lending journey with a PLAYBOOK (corpus modules/05-outreach.md §The playbook, canon T19 col 6): the agent template keeps {hook_line}, {walk} and {lender_notes} as holes, and the plan chooses what fills them from the event. Every sentence lives in lines ONCE — reword step_open_app and every walk that names it changes. A block names lines and never holds text; the first row whose when holds wins and the LAST row has no when, which is what keeps the agent from speaking a literal {hook_line} on a live call. The call square LISTS what it takes, so a block nobody asks for is never evaluated, never in a payload, never in a log. Because the playbook is part of the document it is pinned into the version row at publish: a journey that started on script v1 keeps saying v1, and a wording fix reaches open runs only with on_publish migrate — the property a live vendor registration cannot have (the 17 Sep ruling). walk renders many lines, so publish refuses it mapped to a WhatsApp blank while a call takes it happily.",
